-- A rule that may refuse through a definition three imports away, which
-- the file it imports calls directly: ballot.l4 calls one that
-- residency.l4 defines, and reaches it only through franchise.l4. See
-- boolean-rules.l4 for what an "agreement:" line says, and for `pad`.
--
-- agreement: casts may refuse with ["non-residents are not modelled"]
-- agreement: casts {"adult": true, "resident": true} => answers true
-- agreement: casts {"adult": true, "resident": false} => refuses "non-residents are not modelled"
-- agreement: casts {"adult": false, "resident": true} => answers false
-- agreement: casts {"adult": false, "resident": false} => answers false

IMPORT ballot

@export whether the person casts a ballot
GIVEN adult IS A BOOLEAN
      resident IS A BOOLEAN
      pad IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE casts IF adult AND `the person may cast a ballot` resident
